+## UBU-D0380: User-visible latency includes request ingress before controller acceptance
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §21.1.4. Narrows `UBU-Q0168`; numerical profiles and measured acceptance remain Open.
+
+Bind end-to-end acknowledgment, first-useful-result and total-job ceilings to each route's original offer event before internal queueing. Bound ingress queues and record offer, acceptance/refusal and presentation separately with qualified clocks. Existing class deadlines remain separately observable and intersect the remaining offer budgets; handoff and retries cannot restart user-visible waiting.
+
+Expire or invalidate pending ingress locally and prevent late dispatch/release under the existing fallback, interruption and retention rules. A fast acceptance-relative result cannot qualify as timely after its original offer ceiling. Keep pre-acceptance refusals, expiry and missing outcomes in `UBU-D0361`'s offered-request accounting.
+
+Require §21.1.4's delayed-handoff, ingress-saturation, boundary and interruption fixtures, plus pinned deployment trials driven by frozen arrivals for claimed concurrent/sustained workloads. Report ingress and end-to-end timings alongside class timings; an incompletely offered workload cannot qualify a smaller denominator. These are enforcement and evidence requirements, not numerical selection or passing implementation/hardware evidence. `UBU-Q0168` stays Open pending the existing frozen acceptance trials and operator review; no kernel API or wire-schema change is selected.
+
